BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 730 Tm (Do small businesses actually follow the conventional start-up-growth-maturity-decline life) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 716 Tm (cycle, or do weekly transaction records reveal more heterogeneous paths? We examine whether) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 702 Tm (high-frequency sales data can define economically meaningful life-cycle states for small) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 688 Tm (businesses and whether early signals such as sales trend, drawdown risk, volatility, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 674 Tm (new-customer acquisition help distinguish recovery from persistent decline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 644 Tm (Methodology) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 626 Tm (This study uses weekly transaction records from Korean Credit Data \(KCD\) for 59,089) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 612 Tm (establishments in Seoul's food-service sector. We combine two complementary empirical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 598 Tm (designs. First, for post-entry dynamics, we study recently opened establishments by aligning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 584 Tm (stores by weeks since opening and recovering recurring sales-path patterns from weekly time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 570 Tm (series. We then summarize movement before and after major turning points to assign) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 556 Tm (interpretable trajectory labels such as DDZ and UUX. Second, for the broader stock of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 542 Tm (surviving businesses, we use an observed-window design covering 50,635 establishments with) Tj ET
